  "implemented": [
    "Measure the actual packetized AU including negotiated RTP extensions and conservative wire overhead; measured100-103 completed frame costs match every recorded RTP charge.",
    "Frame admission rechecks the live path target after partial ACKs and rate changes; no self-referential offered-rate floor.",
    "Reserve at most the next16ms of paced AU bytes before its first packet; a large AU remains serialized by the existing RTP pacer instead of first waiting for its entire size to fit a frame-credit window.",
    "Rapid frame-aware admission has one baseline-RTT deadline bounded50-250ms; partial ACKs cannot renew it. Long waits refresh bounded raw-admission leases.",
    "Receipt waits shorter than a media tick preserve the raw capture burst history; pending lease cancellation and close do not pulse the worker.",
    "One future encoded frame held behind the active AU for a media tick applies raw backpressure; two queued frames pause immediately. Receipt and queue owners remain independent. No predictive payloads/references are dropped or rewritten."
  ],
